Compliance Notes
========================================================================

- Components under LGPL (libmodbus) require that you can relink the
  application with a modified version of the library. Ensure your
  distribution method satisfies this obligation before commercial use.

- Components under dual-license (Mbed TLS: Apache-2.0 OR GPL-2.0) allow
  you to choose Apache-2.0 for permissive use.

- ChaN's FatFs license is permissive but requires retention of the
  copyright notice in source distributions.

- All other components use permissive licenses (ISC / MIT / BSD /
  Apache-2.0 / Zlib) compatible with commercial use provided notices
  are retained.

